      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "THE FRISKEE FLASH (7) went forward last time and looked a chance on the corner but weakened to finish sixth over 1400m at Wagga. This offers her a great chance of breaking through. GRAFFI (4) did little and finished ninth over 1500m at Muswellbrook last start after being in contention on the bend, a less impressive effort than her fourth at Scone the run before. Finds a more suitable contest and can take this out. ONA BIVVY (1) returns from a spell of four months and is having his first run for a new yard. Finished eighth at Moe over 1208m when first-up last time in work. Has found a suitable race and is worth including. SOUTH EIGHT (6) was out of the money on debut two runs back then again missed the frame last start when he got a long way back over 1000m at Dubbo, beaten 7 lengths into seventh. Finds an easier assignment and keep safe.",
